   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Re: Mises-Fisher distribution - multidimensional sphere",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Tuesday, June 28, 2016 at 4:11:45 AM UTC-4, Stefano wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Can you do a prediction for NUTS sampling?</div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>I predict it will work fine (evantually).<br> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>If there are the basis, for creating the distribution myself I imagine I have to plug (which is not gonna be really straightforward :) ), is this the right route?</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>The LaTeX didn&#39;t really come through, but it is just the logarithm of<br><br><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/DyOZzIaDQFVthyp5Lmu82l4GdZAX4F3QcfzpKjVRs9rT-fyCQTntJvx2_NOoV48vcSFIwEaJAuHn4A2QUHx8pVRTW-8w21uroYzMPbba3mVh-3bBiq37w37WyM75DgpRFBMflNENbASAxk-NpVZYnbIwQA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/b60fc67076e711242f5a8e097cff9c12bae68499\" style=\"vertical-align:-1.171ex;width:31.535ex;min-height:3.509ex\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle f_{p}(\\mathbf {x} ;{\\boldsymbol {\\mu }},\\kappa )=C_{p}(\\kappa )\\exp \\left({\\kappa {\\boldsymbol {\\mu }}^{T}\\mathbf {x} }\\right)}\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Von_Mises%E2%80%93Fisher_distribution\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Von_Mises%25E2%2580%2593Fisher_distribution&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461036659000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0RpQvF91hnTb6WRRi1aT4r\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Von_Mises%E2%80%93Fisher_distribution</a><br><br>so you have --- for even p ---<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  unit_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><code><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> half_pm1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  half_pm1 = p / 2 - 1; // ignore integer division warning since p is even</span><span style=\"color:#800\"></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  unit_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  target </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dot_product</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> half_pm1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">modified_bessel_first_kind</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">half_pm1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> kappa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>For odd p, you have to reimplement that Bessel function for half-integers.<br><br>Ben<br><br></div></div>\r\n</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
